13) FAILURE CASES — HOW DO WE KNOW SYSTEM IS DOWN?
==============================================================================

This is the perfect next Jordan question.

WHY THIS EXISTS
Partition ownership only works if membership is correct.

If node is dead but ring still routes traffic there:
blackhole.

So we need FAILURE DETECTION.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
A) HEARTBEATS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Each node sends heartbeat:
every 1s → metadata service

Miss 3 heartbeats:
suspect node failure

Problem solved:
fast crash detection

Tradeoff:
false positives during GC pauses

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
B) GOSSIP FAILURE DETECTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Used by:
Cassandra, Dynamo style systems

Nodes exchange:
- membership
- liveness
- load
- token ownership

Why great:
scales to large clusters

Tradeoff:
eventual membership convergence

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
C) PHI ACCRUAL DETECTOR
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Instead of fixed timeout:
probabilistic suspicion score.

Much smarter under network jitter.

Senior interview line:
> modern systems prefer suspicion-based failure detection over hard timeouts.

